{
  "name": "gridrunner-improved",
  "description": "GRIDRUNNER (Jeff Minter / Llamasoft, published by HES, 1982) - the original 8K C64 CARTRIDGE image, $8000-$8FFF. The cartridge header is intact: cold-start vector at $8000, NMI vector at $8002, CBM80 signature at $8004. The seeded reading came from mwenge/matrix, whose file header describes the game as Matrix (1983) and whose binary is a converted PRG with those five signature bytes zeroed and a SYS 2061 BASIC stub added at $0800. The banner this program writes to screen row 0 reads GRIDRUNNER, in the game's own 64-glyph character set at $8E00; run the gridrunnerCharset decoder over any text region to read it. Everything is drawn with characters: no sprites, no raster interrupt, no wait on $D012; the whole game is timed by one counter at $0D and a DEX loop at $83E8. [Description restored by hand into this export: diffProjects emits no meta.set op, so set_project_description reaches the document but never the file.]",
