      "comments": [
        {
          "id": "cmt_kpyfyd",
          "address": "$0002",
          "text": "Scratch column for whatever is being drawn (0-39). Also the low byte of the VIC register pointer in InitializeGame and of the pod screen pointer in MovePodDownOneRow - both bound to their own names at those sites."
        },
        {
          "id": "cmt_438m7h",
          "address": "$0003",
          "text": "Scratch row for whatever is being drawn (0-24). GetLinePtrForCurrentYPosition indexes the line tables with it."
        },
        {
          "id": "cmt_r8kjc3",
          "address": "$0008",
          "text": "The grid column while DrawGrid sweeps, and the high byte of the clear-screen pointer in ClearPlayArea. The seeded project and the reference both call this byte randomValue, on the strength of PlayAnotherSound doing LDA $08 / STA $D401. But PlayAnotherSound is only ever called from inside DrawGrid's two sweeps, where $08 holds the column being drawn - so what goes into the SID is the column, which is why the tone rises across the screen. find_instructions over $0008 shows thirteen sites in three routines and not one of them puts a random number here."
        },
        {
          "id": "cmt_nk4shb",
          "address": "$0009",
          "text": "The grid row while DrawGrid sweeps; the explosion character during the ship materialise sequence. Two unrelated uses of one byte, bound separately."
        },
        {
          "id": "cmt_vje2p3",
          "address": "$000B",
          "text": "The ship's column. The reference calls this previousXPosition, but it is not a previous anything: it is where the ship IS between frames. UpdateShipPosition copies it into the scratch cell, moves, and copies it back; DrawBullet launches from it; the explosion is centred on it."
        },
        {
          "id": "cmt_5esalm",
          "address": "$000C",
          "text": "The ship's row, for the same reason as $0B."
        },
        {
          "id": "cmt_55o4yf",
          "address": "$000D",
          "text": "The master frame counter, and the only clock in the game. UpdateShipPosition decrements it every pass of the main loop; ResetMasterFrameCounter catches the wrap past $FF and reloads $80. The zapper runs when it equals 1 and the background sound on odd values, so every subsystem is phased off this one byte. The reference calls it shipAnimationFrameRate, which describes one of its four readers."
        },
        {
          "id": "cmt_598fzl",
          "address": "$000F",
          "text": "Countdown to the next bullet frame, reloaded with $18. DrawLaser also tests it for the value 5 and UpdateLaserCharacter decrements it a second time, so bullet and laser share the timer. The seeded project had gridYPos here."
        },
        {
          "id": "cmt_aoofo7",
          "address": "$0010",
          "text": "Bullet column. The seeded project had $10 and $11 the wrong way round: DrawBullet stores shipXPosition here and shipYPosition in $11, and it is $11 that carries the $FF no-bullet sentinel."
        },
        {
          "id": "cmt_qc64yv",
          "address": "$0011",
          "text": "Bullet row, or $FF for \"no bullet in flight\"."
        },
        {
          "id": "cmt_h41k0x",
          "address": "$0017",
          "text": "Counts down to the next zapper firing; reloaded from laserFrameRate, the per-level value. UpdatePods also only runs when it happens to equal 5. The seeded project called this laserShootInterval, which is $18."
        },
        {
          "id": "cmt_upncku",
          "address": "$0018",
          "text": "$FF means the lasers are live and DrawLaser should draw them; DrawLaser clears it when the two beams meet."
        },
        {
          "id": "cmt_81hz7s",
          "address": "$0019",
          "text": "The laser animation character, cycling $05/$06. The seeded project called this laserAndPodInterval, which is $17."
        },
        {
          "id": "cmt_ux9z0x",
          "address": "$0021",
          "text": "Counts down to the next pod movement, reloaded with $40. The seeded project called this cyclesToWasteCounter, which is $30."
        },
        {
          "id": "cmt_7x3v5s",
          "address": "$0022",
          "text": "Pitch of the hit sound, swept down from $F0 into voice 3 while its top two bits are set. The seeded project called this soundEffectControl, which is $36."
        },
        {
          "id": "cmt_6th5nl",
          "address": "$0023",
          "text": "How many more times to restart the $22 sweep. Set to 3 by every scoring hit."
        },
        {
          "id": "cmt_xkezr1",
          "address": "$0025",
          "text": "Countdown to the next droid frame, reloaded with $80. The seeded project called this droidsLeftToKill, which is $2A."
        },
        {
          "id": "cmt_h4kxzl",
          "address": "$0026",
          "text": "Current droid animation character, cycling $13/$14/$15. The seeded project called this sizeOfDroidSquadForLevel, which is $2B."
        },
        {
          "id": "cmt_ceewix",
          "address": "$0028",
          "text": "Frames of quiet left before the next droid squad starts, reloaded with $20. The reference has no name for this byte at all - it calls it a28."
        },
        {
          "id": "cmt_kcy5q6",
          "address": "$0029",
          "text": "Segments still to be emitted for the squad currently being built. SpawnDroidSegments appends one per call while this is non-zero and gives the last one the visible bit; the reference calls it a29."
        },
        {
          "id": "cmt_jwu6dg",
          "address": "$002B",
          "text": "Segments per squad for this level, read out of the table at $8CD4 by PrepareNextLevel. The seeded project called this clearScreenLineLoPtr; the clear-screen pointer is $07/$08."
        },
        {
          "id": "cmt_mtb7wr",
          "address": "$0036",
          "text": "Outer counter for the level fanfare, counting down from $30 and doubling as the colour of the level digits. Only reachable at all once the laserFrameRateForLevel region stops swallowing $8D16."
        },
        {
          "id": "cmt_jty4ah",
          "address": "$00C5",
          "text": "KERNAL: matrix code of the key currently pressed, $40 when none. Still maintained because ColdStart re-enables interrupts and leaves the KERNAL IRQ in place. The only code this game looks for is $29 = 41 = P."
        },
        {
          "id": "cmt_xq6y9l",
          "address": "$0340",
          "text": "Low bytes of the 24 screen row addresses, built by InitializeGame. Indexed by row, so every draw in the game is one indexed load from here plus one from $0360."
        },
        {
          "id": "cmt_edgs3r",
          "address": "$040F",
          "text": "The player's score - seven characters of screen RAM on row 0, columns 15-21. There is no score anywhere else in memory: IncrementPlayerScore counts these characters up as text and UpdateHighScore compares them as text."
        },
        {
          "id": "cmt_hopy1g",
          "address": "$041B",
          "text": "The high score, row 0 columns 27-33. Only ever written by UpdateHighScore, digit for digit out of $040F."
        },
        {
          "id": "cmt_vlhgss",
          "address": "$0427",
          "text": "Lives, as a single screen character at row 0 column 39. Set to '4' by StartLevel and by the initial banner byte at $8847, incremented by PrepareNextLevel (capped at '9') and decremented on each death; reaching '0' is game over."
        },
        {
          "id": "cmt_es7vvf",
          "address": "$0557",
          "text": "The two digits of \"ENTER LEVEL nn\" on the title screen, counted up by IncrementSelectedLevel."
        },
        {
          "id": "cmt_3mxci8",
          "address": "$055E",
          "text": "The two digits of \"ENTER GRID AREA nn\" on the interstitial, counted up by IncrementLevelDigits."
        },
        {
          "id": "cmt_h6dbvp",
          "address": "$0FFF",
          "text": "Base-1 of the 32 pod screen-pointer low bytes at $1000-$101F. Only slots 1-24 are ever used."
        },
        {
          "id": "cmt_bsrclm",
          "address": "$101F",
          "text": "Base-1 of the 32 pod screen-pointer high bytes at $1020-$103F. $FF marks a free slot."
        },
        {
          "id": "cmt_jpgngf",
          "address": "$10FF",
          "text": "Base-1 of the droid column array. Entry 1 is the head of the chain; each higher entry follows the one below it."
        },
        {
          "id": "cmt_eibmz1",
          "address": "$12FF",
          "text": "Base-1 of the droid status array. Bit $80 = visible/alive, bit $40 = this segment steers for itself (the head), bits $01/$02 = which way it is going."
        },
        {
          "id": "cmt_qtkkn1",
          "address": "$1500",
          "text": "Explosion fragment columns, entries 1-8."
        },
        {
          "id": "cmt_74eydj",
          "address": "$1600",
          "text": "Explosion fragment rows, entries 1-8."
        },
        {
          "id": "cmt_7027kw",
          "address": "$DC11",
          "text": "CIA 1 port B, reached through the chip's 16-byte register mirror ($DC01 + $10). This is JOYSTICK PORT 1; port 2 is port A at $DC00. The reference's comment on the title-screen read at $8DB0 says port 2."
        },
        {
          "id": "cmt_ou53mk",
          "address": "$002C",
          "text": "No instruction in the program touches $2C. The seeded project named it clearScreenLineHiPtr; the clear-screen pointer is $07/$08. remove_label refuses to delete it (\"comes from user rather than from this project\"), so it is renamed instead."
        }
      ]
    },
